1. Evaluate the first term, ${\left({\frac{8}{27}}\right)^{-\frac{1}{3}}}$:
   \begin{align*}
   \left({\frac{8}{27}}\right)^{-\frac{1}{3}} &= \left({\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^3}\right)^{-\frac{1}{3}} \\
   &= \left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{3 \times \left(-\frac{1}{3}\right)} \\
   &= \left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{-1} \\
