(2) Solution: According to the expression $f(x)=x-\frac{1}{x}$, the original equation becomes: $2^{t}\cdot (4^{t}-\frac{1}{4^{t}})-m(2^{t}-\frac{1}{2^{t}})=0$;
Simplifying, we get $(2^{2t})^{2}-m\cdot 2^{2t}+m-1=0$;
Thus, $(2^{2t}-1)[2^{2t}-(m-1)]=0$  $(①)$;
Since $t\in[1,2]$;
Thus, $2^{2t}\in[4,16]$;
Hence, $2^{2t}-1 > 0$;
Therefore, from equation $(①)$, we get $2^{2t}-(m-1)=0$;
Thus, $m-1=2^{2t}$;
